\ A raise inside a prelude compound reached through non-tail user words, so one chain crosses
\ source files: the raising native and its prelude callers render src/prelude.1z rows above the
\ user-file rows. Pinned interpreted; the AOT suite builds this file through a `.source` redirect
\ and renders the same chain. The eager tier drops the `say` row, recorded in
\ spec/bugs/20260815-eager-drops-mid-chain-compiled-frame.md, so this file does not pin it.

say: ( v -- ) [ print-line 0 drop ] ;
report: ( v -- ) [ say 0 drop ] ;

